% c137 (texture; Adler ch. 16, PDF 229: two colours doubling at pitch swallow each other): 126 Bn 1's counter C4-G3 (was C4-D4, a half note in unison with the violas' melody D4); it no longer meets the melody, and avoids the octaves C-B with the cellos.
% c181 (A&S Unit 20, PDF 330-331 section 4 and PDF 343 point 8; the c-comment above on 126 already warned that G3 makes fifths): 126 Bn 1 D4-A3 on beats 3-4 (was G3 half),
% A3 taken early and tied into 127, so its counter no longer moves G3/D4 -> A3/E4 in fifths with the violas' F2: the fifth A3/E4 is reached by oblique motion (A&S PDF 342, Ex. 20-27).
